{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"candidate_id\": \"4e8277b63073a5e770e39dc2e62ad2171c2ad08abd1ec36b88326fe8f078c052\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    \"Read original schematic, PCB and requirements; confirmed their hashes match the packet.\",\n    \"Freshly exported native schematic connectivity using KiCad 10.0.7 and independently traced saved front copper from J1.1 through R1 to J1.2, including the /OUT T junction.\",\n    \"Inspected placement, outline, tracks, via and saved ground zone; reviewed native ERC/DRC reports, ignored checks and geometry records.\",\n    \"Calculated R1 continuous dissipation with the specified external source and clamp. Structural checks contain no stimulus or power assessment for this condition.\"\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"defect\",\n      \"condition\": \"/IN held at 48 V DC and /OUT externally clamped to 0 V indefinitely.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Line 1: external voltage/clamp condition and fitted R1 continuous limit of 0.1 W\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/requirements.txt\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"R1 instance, UUID c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78; lines 1261–1285: fitted, value 10k\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"R1 pads, lines 359–373; J1 pads, lines 587–613; saved /IN and /OUT copper, lines 667–697\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"nets /IN and /OUT: R1.1 connects to J1.1; R1.2 connects to J1.2\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/design.xml\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"verified_routes and calculation: R1_current_A=0.0048, R1_power_W=0.2304, limit_ratio=2.304\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-results.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"physical-001\",\n      \"location\": \"R1, saved PCB position (105, 100) mm, between /IN and /OUT\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"The maintained voltage across the nominal 10 kΩ resistor produces continuous dissipation P=(48−0)²/10000=0.2304 W, exceeding its stated 0.1 W continuous limit by 0.1304 W.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Saved copper provides the input path to R1.1 and the return from R1.2 through J1.2 to the external clamp. The clamp prevents /OUT from charging toward /IN, so this dissipation persists. R1 operates at 2.304 times the specified continuous limit. The capacitor and ground pour do not remove the maintained resistor voltage. This establishes a power-limit violation without assuming a package rating, operating temperature or failure time.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"R1 dissipates 0.2304 W against its 0.1 W continuous limit\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"No hardware measurements, thermal simulation, temperature or failure-time prediction, or copper ampacity qualification were performed.\",\n    \"Saved zone fill was inspected without refilling. Ignored ERC/DRC categories were not independently rerun; no fabrication capability audit or assembly inspection was performed.\",\n    \"Analysis uses native nominal resistance and the stipulated external holding/clamping condition. Other operating conditions, component ratings, tolerances and ECU qualification were outside scope.\",\n    \"Commands, versions, assumptions and outcomes are recorded in review-work/physical/experiments/README.md and commands.json.\"\n  ],\n  \"packet_sha256\": \"2e7bae6999033e125901d43722e04b851be590cc6ea1dab4a734f7e44ac6237a\",\n  \"role\": \"physical\",\n  \"run_id\": \"b016daf9-1004-4fab-9e04-8df3be3a541b\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.review/1\"\n}"}}
